/*!
    \qmltype ClayCanvas
    \inqmlmodule Clayground.Canvas
    \brief A 2D canvas with world coordinate mapping and camera controls.

    ClayCanvas provides a complete 2D rendering system with world unit coordinates,
    viewport management, camera following, and debug visualization. It transforms
    between screen pixels and world units automatically.

    The coordinate system uses Y-up orientation (like standard math coordinates).

    Example usage:
    \qml
    import Clayground.Canvas as Canv

    Canv.ClayCanvas {
        id: canvas
        anchors.fill: parent
        worldXMin: -10; worldXMax: 10
        worldYMin: -10; worldYMax: 10
        pixelPerUnit: 50
        observedItem: player
    }
    \endqml

    \section1 Properties

    \qmlproperty real ClayCanvas::deviceScalingFactor
    Automatic scaling factor based on device height (height / 1080).

    \qmlproperty real ClayCanvas::zoomFactor
    Zoom level multiplier. Default is 1.0.

    \qmlproperty real ClayCanvas::pixelPerUnit
    Number of screen pixels per world unit.

    \qmlproperty bool ClayCanvas::interactive
    Whether the canvas viewport can be panned interactively.

    \qmlproperty real ClayCanvas::worldXMin
    Minimum X coordinate boundary in world units.

    \qmlproperty real ClayCanvas::worldXMax
    Maximum X coordinate boundary in world units.

    \qmlproperty real ClayCanvas::worldYMin
    Minimum Y coordinate boundary in world units.

    \qmlproperty real ClayCanvas::worldYMax
    Maximum Y coordinate boundary in world units.

    \qmlproperty real ClayCanvas::xInWU
    \readonly
    Current viewport left edge position in world units.

    \qmlproperty real ClayCanvas::yInWU
    \readonly
    Current viewport top edge position in world units.

    \qmlproperty real ClayCanvas::sWidthInWU
    \readonly
    Viewport width in world units.

    \qmlproperty real ClayCanvas::sHeightInWU
    \readonly
    Viewport height in world units.

    \qmlproperty real ClayCanvas::viewPortCenterWuX
    X coordinate of viewport center in world units.

    \qmlproperty real ClayCanvas::viewPortCenterWuY
    Y coordinate of viewport center in world units.

    \qmlproperty bool ClayCanvas::showDebugInfo
    Whether to show the debug overlay with coordinate grid. Toggle with Space key.

    \qmlproperty bool ClayCanvas::keyBoardNavigationEnabled
    Enable keyboard navigation (IJKL for pan, E/D for zoom).

    \qmlproperty Item ClayCanvas::coordSys
    \readonly
    The coordinate system container. Child items should be parented to this.

    \qmlproperty var ClayCanvas::observedItem
    Item that the camera follows automatically. Set to null to disable following.

    \section1 Methods

    \qmlmethod real ClayCanvas::xToScreen(real xCart)
    Converts a world X coordinate to screen X coordinate.

    \qmlmethod real ClayCanvas::screenXToWorld(real xScr)
    Converts a screen X coordinate to world X coordinate.

    \qmlmethod real ClayCanvas::yToScreen(real yCart)
    Converts a world Y coordinate to screen Y coordinate.

    \qmlmethod real ClayCanvas::screenYToWorld(real yScr)
    Converts a screen Y coordinate to world Y coordinate.

    \qmlmethod void ClayCanvas::fit(real xMin, real yMin, real xMax, real yMax, real marginWu)
    Frames the world rectangle (xMin, yMin) to (xMax, yMax): sets pixelPerUnit so
    the rectangle plus marginWu on each side fills the view with its aspect ratio
    kept, centers the viewport on it and stops following observedItem. marginWu is
    optional and defaults to 0.

    \section1 Signals

    \qmlsignal ClayCanvas::keyPressed(var event)
    Emitted when a key is pressed while the canvas has focus.

    \qmlsignal ClayCanvas::keyReleased(var event)
    Emitted when a key is released while the canvas has focus.
*/

/*!
    \qmltype Rectangle
    \inqmlmodule Clayground.Canvas
    \brief A rectangle positioned and sized in world units.

    Rectangle extends Qt Quick's Rectangle to work with ClayCanvas world coordinates.
    Position and size are specified in world units, automatically transformed to screen coordinates.

    Example usage:
    \qml
    import Clayground.Canvas as Canv

    Canv.Rectangle {
        canvas: myCanvas
        xWu: 5; yWu: 3
        widthWu: 2; heightWu: 1
        color: "red"
    }
    \endqml

    \section1 Properties

    \qmlproperty ClayCanvas Rectangle::canvas
    The parent canvas for coordinate transformation. Required.

    \qmlproperty real Rectangle::xWu
    X position in world units.

    \qmlproperty real Rectangle::yWu
    Y position in world units.

    \qmlproperty real Rectangle::widthWu
    Width in world units.

    \qmlproperty real Rectangle::heightWu
    Height in world units.
*/

/*!
    \qmltype Image
    \inqmlmodule Clayground.Canvas
    \brief An image positioned and sized in world units.

    Image extends Qt Quick's Image to work with ClayCanvas world coordinates.
    Position and size are specified in world units, with the image scaled to fit.

    Example usage:
    \qml
    import Clayground.Canvas as Canv

    Canv.Image {
        canvas: myCanvas
        xWu: -5; yWu: 5
        widthWu: 3; heightWu: 3
        source: "player.png"
    }
    \endqml

    \section1 Properties

    \qmlproperty ClayCanvas Image::canvas
    The parent canvas for coordinate transformation. Required.

    \qmlproperty real Image::xWu
    X position in world units.

    \qmlproperty real Image::yWu
    Y position in world units.

    \qmlproperty real Image::widthWu
    Width in world units.

    \qmlproperty real Image::heightWu
    Height in world units.
*/

/*!
    \qmltype Text
    \inqmlmodule Clayground.Canvas
    \brief Text element positioned in world units with scalable font size.

    Text extends Qt Quick's Text to work with ClayCanvas world coordinates.
    Position and font size are specified in world units.

    Example usage:
    \qml
    import Clayground.Canvas as Canv

    Canv.Text {
        canvas: myCanvas
        xWu: 0; yWu: 2
        fontSizeWu: 0.5
        text: "Hello World!"
        color: "blue"
    }
    \endqml

    \section1 Properties

    \qmlproperty ClayCanvas Text::canvas
    The parent canvas for coordinate transformation. Required.

    \qmlproperty real Text::xWu
    X position in world units.

    \qmlproperty real Text::yWu
    Y position in world units.

    \qmlproperty real Text::fontSizeWu
    Font size in world units.

    \qmlproperty string Text::sketch
    Pen used for the text: "none" (default), "chalk" or "marker". Both sketch pens
    switch font.family to the hand font the plugin ships; "chalk" adds a faint
    offset copy as grain.

    \qmlproperty real Text::progress
    How much of the text is written, from 0 to 1 (default 1). Whole characters are
    revealed from the left. Single line text; a wrapped text is revealed by width only.

    \qmlproperty int Text::shownCharacters
    \readonly
    Number of characters currently shown, ceil(progress * text.length).

    \qmlproperty string Text::handFont
    \readonly
    Family name of the hand font shipped with the plugin, empty until it is loaded.
*/

/*!
    \qmltype Poly
    \inqmlmodule Clayground.Canvas
    \brief A polygon or polyline shape defined by vertices in world units.

    Poly renders a shape from an array of vertex points in world coordinates.
    It can display as a closed polygon (with fill) or an open polyline.

    Example usage:
    \qml
    import Clayground.Canvas as Canv

    Canv.Poly {
        canvas: myCanvas
        vertices: [
            {x: 0, y: 0},
            {x: 2, y: 0},
            {x: 1, y: 2}
        ]
        fillColor: "green"
        strokeColor: "darkgreen"
    }
    \endqml

    \section1 Properties

    \qmlproperty ClayCanvas Poly::canvas
    The parent canvas for coordinate transformation. Required.

    \qmlproperty var Poly::vertices
    Array of vertex points {x, y} in world units.

    \qmlproperty real Poly::strokeWidth
    Width of the outline stroke in pixels.

    \qmlproperty color Poly::strokeColor
    Color of the outline stroke.

    \qmlproperty color Poly::fillColor
    Fill color. Use "transparent" for polyline (no fill).

    \qmlproperty ShapePath.StrokeStyle Poly::strokeStyle
    Style of the stroke (solid, dash, etc.).

    \qmlproperty var Poly::dashPattern
    Custom dash pattern as an array of dash/gap lengths.

    \qmlproperty bool Poly::closed
    \readonly
    Whether the shape is closed. True when fillColor is not transparent.

    \qmlproperty string Poly::sketch
    Pen used for the outline: "none" (default), "chalk" or "marker". "chalk" draws a
    wobbly, slightly jagged line plus a wider, fainter grain pass; "marker" draws a
    smooth slow wobble with round caps and joins. The vertices stay exact.

    \qmlproperty real Poly::progress
    How much of the outline is drawn, from 0 to 1 (default 1), measured along its
    length from the first vertex.

    \qmlproperty int Poly::seed
    Which wobble the sketch pens use (default 0). Same seed and same vertices draw
    the same line.

    \section1 Methods

    \qmlmethod void Poly::refresh()
    Refreshes the shape visualization after vertex changes.
*/

/*!
    \qmltype Connector
    \inqmlmodule Clayground.Canvas
    \brief A visual line connecting two items with automatic position tracking.

    Connector draws a line between the centers of two items and automatically
    updates when either item moves. Useful for visualizing relationships or
    connections in diagrams and games.

    Example usage:
    \qml
    import Clayground.Canvas as Canv

    Canv.Connector {
        from: nodeA
        to: nodeB
        color: "green"
        strokeWidth: 3
        style: ShapePath.DashLine
    }
    \endqml

    \section1 Properties

    \qmlproperty ClayCanvas Connector::canvas
    The canvas the connector belongs to (default null). When set, the connector pans
    and zooms with the world and its ends may be world points.

    \qmlproperty var Connector::from
    The source: an item (its center is used) or a world point {x, y}, which needs
    canvas to be set. Required.

    \qmlproperty var Connector::to
    The target: an item (its center is used) or a world point {x, y}, which needs
    canvas to be set. Required.

    \qmlproperty string Connector::attach
    Where the line meets an end that is an item: "center" (default) or "edge", the
    edge of the item's bounding box.

    \qmlproperty string Connector::arrow
    Which ends carry an arrow head: "none" (default), "to", "from" or "both".

    \qmlproperty real Connector::headSize
    Length of an arrow head in pixels, 4 * strokeWidth + 4 by default.

    \qmlproperty real Connector::strokeWidth
    Width of the connector line.

    \qmlproperty color Connector::color
    Color of the connector line.

    \qmlproperty ShapePath.StrokeStyle Connector::style
    Style of the line (solid, dash, etc.).

    \qmlproperty var Connector::dashPattern
    Custom dash pattern as an array of dash/gap lengths.

    \qmlproperty string Connector::sketch
    Pen used for the line and the heads: "none" (default), "chalk" or "marker", as
    on Poly.

    \qmlproperty real Connector::progress
    How much of the connector is drawn, from 0 to 1 (default 1), in the order shaft,
    head at to, head at from.

    \qmlproperty int Connector::seed
    Which wobble the sketch pens use (default 0).
*/

/*!
    \qmltype Axes
    \inqmlmodule Clayground.Canvas
    \brief An x and a y axis out of one origin, with labels and an optional series.

    Axes draws two arrow-headed axes from a common origin, a label at the end of
    each, and an optional series of points on them. Everything is placed in world
    units, so the axes pan and zoom with the canvas like any other canvas item.

    With progress below 1 the parts draw themselves in order: x axis, y axis,
    x label, y label, series - each part priced by the ink it costs, so a
    progress of 0.5 is half the drawing and not the third part of five.

    Example usage:
    \qml
    import Clayground.Canvas as Canv

    Canv.Axes {
        canvas: myCanvas
        xWu: 1; yWu: 1
        widthWu: 5; heightWu: 3
        xLabel: "Ib"; yLabel: "Ic"
        series: [{x: 1.4, y: 1.2}, {x: 3.0, y: 2.0}, {x: 5.5, y: 3.4}]
        sketch: "chalk"
        strokeColor: "#f1efe6"
    }
    \endqml

    \section1 Properties

    \qmlproperty ClayCanvas Axes::canvas
    The parent canvas for coordinate transformation. Required.

    \qmlproperty real Axes::xWu
    X position of the origin in world units.

    \qmlproperty real Axes::yWu
    Y position of the origin in world units.

    \qmlproperty real Axes::widthWu
    Length of the x axis in world units.

    \qmlproperty real Axes::heightWu
    Length of the y axis in world units.

    \qmlproperty string Axes::xLabel
    Label drawn at the end of the x axis.

    \qmlproperty string Axes::yLabel
    Label drawn at the end of the y axis.

    \qmlproperty real Axes::fontSizeWu
    Font size of the labels in world units. Default is 0.4.

    \qmlproperty var Axes::series
    Array of points {x, y} in world units drawn as a polyline on the axes. Empty by
    default.

    \qmlproperty color Axes::strokeColor
    Color of the axes and the labels. Default is black.

    \qmlproperty real Axes::strokeWidth
    Width of the axis lines in pixels. Default is 2.

    \qmlproperty color Axes::seriesColor
    Color of the series line. Defaults to strokeColor.

    \qmlproperty real Axes::seriesWidth
    Width of the series line in pixels. Defaults to strokeWidth.

    \qmlproperty real Axes::headSize
    Length of an axis arrow head in pixels, 4 * strokeWidth + 4 by default.

    \qmlproperty string Axes::sketch
    Pen used for the axes, labels and series: "none" (default), "chalk" or "marker",
    as on Poly.

    \qmlproperty real Axes::progress
    How much of the drawing is done, from 0 to 1 (default 1), spent in the order x
    axis, y axis, x label, y label, series.

    \qmlproperty int Axes::seed
    Which wobble the sketch pens use (default 0).

    \qmlproperty var Axes::fractions
    \readonly
    The five part fractions at the current progress, in the order x axis, y axis, x
    label, y label, series.
*/
